MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Crossroads Guitar Festival 2013 feels like a natural next choice because my recent Clapton and Hendrix listening has me interested in expressive guitar playing and blues-rock performances.",
    "Uncaged and Ultimate Waylon Jennings fit the country side of my listening, while Roy Orbison's soulful vocals also appeal to me, even though none is my strongest choice today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Vogues and Gary Lewis collections lean toward pop when I currently want blues and guitar-driven music; being familiar older music does not make them equally appealing.",
    "Good Times! and Mono give me too little information to connect them with my interests, and I rarely try something unless I have a clear reason to expect a match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to treat an interest in established performers as a broad interest in older pop and greatest-hits collections.",
    "My occasional interest in country seems to carry more weight than my stronger desire for blues-oriented guitar music on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my Clapton and Hendrix listening matters especially now: guitar playing and blues influence are stronger reasons to choose than a shared era.",
    "A loose match is usually not enough for me to act. Terraplane interests me if it is Steve Earle's blues album, but Crossroads gives me the clearest reason to make my one choice today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized some of my roots and country interests, but broadened them too far beyond the blues and guitar performances I most want right now."
}
